      "writtenOn": "2023-10-26T08:07:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What is special about creation of this instance ?\n\nDevelopers often assume it\u0027s fine to initialize mutable stuff in the constructor and use it on another thread. This is explicitly NOT fine according to the java spec. `final` is the modifier that makes this okay.\n\nIn this patch, you don\u0027t have this problem, but I am worried that the comment will make developers think this is fine. In fact, I think attention should be drawn instead on the fact that it\u0027s not okay to rely on this. I\u0027ll add more comments on this later on in this patch ; for now let\u0027s remove the \"after the creation...\" in this sentence.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 90,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 90,
        "endChar": 39
      },
      "revId": "fd18490ce8a2224148cb762697ec5e5850e32595",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
